12
00:32:30,967 --> 00:32:36,967
Christmas is an annual festival commemorating the birth of Jesus Christ, observed primarily on December
25 as a religious and cultural celebration among billions of people around the world.

13
00:35:13,548 --> 00:35:19,548
A liturgical feast central to Christianity, Christmas
preparation begins on the First Sunday of Advent.

14
00:37:56,129 --> 00:38:02,129
This is followed by Christmastide, which historically in the West
lasts twelve days and culminates on Twelfth Night.

15
00:40:38,709 --> 00:40:44,709
Christmas Day is a public holiday in many countries and is observed by a majority of Christians; it is also
celebrated culturally by many non-Christians and forms an integral part of the annual holiday season.

16
00:43:21,290 --> 00:43:27,290
The traditional Christmas narrative recounted in the New Testament, known as the Nativity of
Jesus, says that Jesus was born in Bethlehem, in accordance with messianic prophecies.

17
00:46:03,870 --> 00:46:09,870
When Joseph and Mary arrived in the city, the inn had no room, and so they were offered a stable where the Christ
Child was soon born, with angels proclaiming this news to shepherds, who then spread the word.

18
00:48:46,451 --> 00:48:52,451
There are different hypotheses regarding the date of the birth of Jesus.

19
00:51:29,032 --> 00:51:35,032
In the early fourth century, the church fixed the date as December 25,
the date of the winter solstice in the Roman Empire.

20
00:54:11,612 --> 00:54:17,612
It is nine months after Annunciation on March 25, also
the Roman date of the spring equinox.

21
00:56:54,193 --> 00:57:00,193
Most Christians celebrate on December 25 in the Gregorian calendar, which has been adopted
almost universally in the civil calendars used in countries throughout the world.

22
00:59:36,774 --> 00:59:42,774
However, part of the Eastern Christian Churches celebrate Christmas on December 25 of the older
Julian calendar, which currently corresponds to January 7 in the Gregorian calendar.

23
01:02:19,354 --> 01:02:25,354
For Christians, celebrating that God came into the world in the form of man to atone for the
sins of humanity is more important than knowing Jesus Christ's exact birth date.

24
01:05:01,935 --> 01:05:07,935
The customs associated with Christmas in various countries have a mix of
pre-Christian, Christian, and secular themes and origins.

25
01:07:44,516 --> 01:07:50,516
Popular holiday traditions include gift-giving; completing an Advent calendar or Advent wreath; Christmas music and carolling; watching Christmas films; viewing a Nativity play; an exchange of Christmas cards;
attending church services; a special meal; and displaying various Christmas decorations, including Christmas trees, Christmas lights, nativity scenes, poinsettias, garlands, wreaths, mistletoe, and holly.

26
01:10:27,096 --> 01:10:33,096
Additionally, several related and often interchangeable figures, known as Santa Claus, Father Christmas, Saint Nicholas, and Christkind,
are associated with bringing gifts to children during the Christmas season and have their own body of traditions and lore.

27
01:13:09,677 --> 01:13:15,677
Because gift-giving and many other aspects of the Christmas festival involve heightened economic activity,
Christmas has become a significant event and a key sales period for retailers and businesses.

28
01:15:52,258 --> 01:15:58,258
Over the past few centuries, Christmas has had a steadily
growing economic effect in many regions of the world.

29
01:18:34,838 --> 01:18:40,838
The film explores themes of holiday, reindeer, christmas.

30
01:21:17,419 --> 01:21:23,419
The tone is emotional.
